70 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 41 0 R/E(Hi, I\220m Leanne \204 mum of two \(and two very excited cocker spaniels\), Doula, Hypnobirthing teacher, Perinatal Yoga teacher, and, yes, I\220ve been cheekily dubbed the \215Queen of Biomechanics\216 by our local homebirth team!)/Pg 11 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

71 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 41 0 R/E(I absolutely love helping parents understand how their bodies really work in pregnancy and birth. When you know how your pelvis, ligaments, and muscles move together, you can use positions, movements, and gentle exercises to make labour more efficient, reduce discomfort, and help your baby get into the best position for birth.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

72 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 41 0 R/E(This is where birth ball work, perinatal yoga, and simple movement techniques come in. From rocking, leaning, and squatting to supported stretches =, use of rebozo and gentle strengthening, these tools help you work with your body, not against it. They can ease tension, open the pelvis, and encourage optimal fetal positioning, making birth feel smoother and more comfortable.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

73 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 41 0 R/E(My goal is to empower you to move confidently, know which positions support you in labour, and feel strong, calm, and connected to your body \204 whether you\220re planning a home birth, birth centre, or hospital birth.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

