<</Title(Always check whether it is comfortable with the birthing person)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 663 0 R/Prev 688 0 R>>
endobj

676 0 obj
<</Title(Whilst facing forwards, place one foot on a chair or stool to your side, toes pointing away from your body \(90 degree angle\))/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 635 0 R/Prev 664 0 R/Next 689 0 R>>
endobj

677 0 obj
<</Title(You can rest your foot on the floor between contractions if required.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 635 0 R/Prev 690 0 R/Next 665 0 R>>
endobj

678 0 obj
<</Title(Feel for the triangular bone on the back of the pelvis.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 631 0 R/Prev 666 0 R/Next 679 0 R>>
endobj

679 0 obj
<</Title(Placing your entire palm flat onto the bone \(there may be a tendency to put more weight into the heel of the palm\), you will press directly down into the sacrum.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 631 0 R/Prev 678 0 R/Next 667 0 R>>
endobj

680 0 obj
<</Title(Move towards the edge of the bed until your bump extends over the edge.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 634 0 R/Prev 668 0 R/Next 681 0 R>>
endobj

681 0 obj
<</Title(Flex your toes up towards your knees and allow your top leg to hang over the bed. Remain in this position for 3 contractions or 10 minutes.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 634 0 R/Prev 680 0 R/Next 669 0 R>>
endobj

682 0 obj
<</Title(Avoid if you suffer from:)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 669 0 R>>
endobj

683 0 obj
<</Title(Kneel on the edge of a couch, bed, or chair.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 640 0 R/Prev 670 0 R/Next 691 0 R>>
endobj

684 0 obj
<</Title(Take two breaths here, then sit on your heels.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 640 0 R/Prev 692 0 R/Next 671 0 R>>
endobj

685 0 obj
<</Title(Adopt an all-fours position or lean over a counter.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 641 0 R/Prev 672 0 R/Next 693 0 R>>
endobj

686 0 obj
<</Title(Jiggle for up to 20 minutes, depending om comfort.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 641 0 R/Prev 694 0 R/Next 673 0 R>>
endobj

687 0 obj
<</Title(The sifting movement helps to relax abdominal muscles to encourage optimal fetal position. It can provide comfort in labour and encourage baby\220s head to descend into the pelvis.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 663 0 R/Prev 674 0 R/Next 695 0 R>>
endobj

688 0 obj
<</Title(Cycle for up to 20 minutes, depending on comfort.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 663 0 R/Prev 696 0 R/Next 675 0 R>>
endobj

689 0 obj
<</Title(During a contraction, gently rock towards your bent knee beyond your foot.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 635 0 R/Prev 676 0 R/Next 690 0 R>>
endobj

690 0 obj
<</Title(A birth partner can stand close or in front for support if needed.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 635 0 R/Prev 689 0 R/Next 677 0 R>>
endobj

691 0 obj
<</Title(With the help of your partner, carefully lower yourself to your hands on the floor and then lower further to rest on your forearms.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 640 0 R/Prev 683 0 R/Next 697 0 R>>
endobj

692 0 obj
<</Title(With the support of your partner, come back up on to your hands, then up to a high kneeling position.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 640 0 R/Prev 698 0 R/Next 684 0 R>>
endobj

